WEBVTT

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.300
I decided I would put it to slumber,
quietly and eternally.

00:00:10.610 --> 00:00:14.340
So even now, this forest presents
an unyielding rampart of briars...

00:00:14.810 --> 00:00:17.470
...and continues to deny entry from the outside.

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:24.820
And it will probably do so
until the time of my death.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:38.130
Maria Watches Over Us

00:01:56.540 --> 00:02:00.950
The Forest of Briars

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:07.450
Rosa Gigantea did?

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:11.690
Rosa Gigantea?

00:02:11.930 --> 00:02:13.790
The Forest of Briars
Suga Sei

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:20.890
It will be Christmas once the exams are over.

00:02:22.570 --> 00:02:25.940
Rosa Foetida mentioned
there would be a party...

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:28.070
...at the Rose Mansion for the closing ceremony.

00:02:30.880 --> 00:02:32.570
Is something the matter?

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:36.980
Onee-sama?

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:40.380
I don't like Christmas.

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:45.160
Would you like covers on these?

00:02:45.460 --> 00:02:46.220
No, thank you.

00:02:49.060 --> 00:02:49.500
The Forest of Briars
Suga Sei

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.200
The Forest of Briars
Suga Sei
So this is what everyone is talking about...

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:51.600
The Forest of Briars
Suga Sei

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:55.830
I wonder if it is better not to, after all.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:57.500
Better not to read it.

00:02:57.810 --> 00:02:58.360
What?

00:02:59.770 --> 00:03:01.140
What are your thoughts, Yumi?

00:03:01.680 --> 00:03:04.170
As for me... I'm going to read it.

00:03:04.410 --> 00:03:07.610
I'm curious, so I'll at least read through it once.

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.310
What if what you read unmistakably
has to do with Rosa Gigantea?

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:13.580
What?

00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:17.330
If Suga Sei turns out to be Rosa Gigantea,

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:18.850
I will probably have great respect for her.

00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.550
Maybe I'll ask her to sign my copy.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.990
I like how you can think like that.

00:03:28.340 --> 00:03:32.200
My Onee-sama really is hesitant
about reading this book...

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:33.470
The Forest of Briars
Suga Sei

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:34.580
The Forest of Briars
Suga Sei
"The Forest of Briars."

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:34.880
The Forest of Briars
Suga Sei

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:37.570
The Forest of Briars
Suga Sei
Its author, Suga Sei, is actually...

00:03:38.280 --> 00:03:39.540
Rosa Gigantea.

00:03:40.180 --> 00:03:44.290
Yes, Rosa Gigantea put
out a confessional novel...

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:47.020
that relates her hidden past
in unreserved fashion...

00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.090
That's the rumor that's going around.

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:54.720
In the end, it's just a rumor, right?

00:03:55.460 --> 00:03:58.370
Started by the people who saw the
article introducing new titles...

00:03:58.370 --> 00:04:00.100
...in this Cosmos Circular.

00:04:00.440 --> 00:04:02.700
Cosmos Circular

00:04:03.770 --> 00:04:06.710
"'The Forest of Briars,' by Suga Sei."

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:11.710
"Were those few months spent
at the academy a dream?"

00:04:12.480 --> 00:04:16.640
"Sei locked away everything in
a forest of briars in her heart"?

00:04:17.250 --> 00:04:21.120
"A shocking autobiographical debut
piece by a promising new author."

00:04:21.720 --> 00:04:25.250
Suga Sei and Rosa Gigantea's
real name, Sato Sei,

00:04:25.360 --> 00:04:27.230
definitely share the same "Sei."

00:04:27.400 --> 00:04:29.760
And if it's autobiographical,

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:33.060
it means she wrote about her
own past in this novel...

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:36.200
So, I can understand how the
rumor got started, but...

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:39.130
Rosa Gigantea's past...

00:04:43.480 --> 00:04:46.470
Since you're first-year students,
I doubt either of you know,

00:04:46.780 --> 00:04:50.380
but Rosa Gigantea's past is...
I guess you could say taboo.

00:04:50.490 --> 00:04:52.150
People try to steer clear of it.

00:04:52.590 --> 00:04:53.550
What do you mean?

00:04:54.020 --> 00:04:56.190
It's like an unspoken agreement.

00:04:56.190 --> 00:04:58.390
Those who know of the
circumstances all keep quiet...

00:04:58.390 --> 00:05:00.830
...and have a way about them,
like they're being protective.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:02.630
I wonder what happened.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.000
Who knows? I was a first-year student,

00:05:06.000 --> 00:05:07.970
so I wasn't told the particulars.

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:11.230
The past... But it's about last year, right?

00:05:12.970 --> 00:05:13.740
Yes.

00:05:14.140 --> 00:05:18.450
If Rosa Gigantea's past is written in this book,

00:05:18.450 --> 00:05:20.940
maybe it's not surprising that
Sachiko-sama is hesitant to read it.

00:05:24.090 --> 00:05:27.860
And then, Sei and Kaori, who were best friends,

00:05:27.860 --> 00:05:30.550
are almost separated from
each other by the adults,

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:34.330
so on Christmas night,
they leave on an aimless journey.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.660
The two had planned to die,

00:05:38.600 --> 00:05:41.040
but when Sei woke up in the hospital,

00:05:41.040 --> 00:05:43.230
Kaori had already gone to Heaven.

00:05:44.010 --> 00:05:46.060
It was a pretty typical ending.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:49.500
Yoshino-san, you didn't cry,
even when you got to the end?

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:55.480
Parts of it even reminded me
of Sachiko-sama and me, so...

00:05:56.350 --> 00:06:00.340
Well, what I wanted to talk about
wasn't the contents of the novel.

00:06:00.490 --> 00:06:02.290
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:06:03.120 --> 00:06:04.730
After reading this,

00:06:04.730 --> 00:06:07.920
I can see why it's rumored that
the author is Rosa Gigantea.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:11.520
I mean, I can't imagine the setting
being any place but Lillian.

00:06:12.570 --> 00:06:16.340
So anyway, Rei-chan apparently read it too,

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:19.700
and she said, "I'm washing
my hands of this matter."

00:06:20.310 --> 00:06:21.000
What?!

00:06:21.180 --> 00:06:23.970
She said she's going to pretend
she never read the novel.

00:06:24.410 --> 00:06:27.970
And that she also doesn't want
to be involved with the rumor.

00:06:28.750 --> 00:06:32.780
Come to think of it,
Sachiko-sama bought the book,

00:06:33.290 --> 00:06:35.410
but she also seemed reluctant to read it.

00:06:36.260 --> 00:06:37.820
I wonder what happened...

00:06:38.660 --> 00:06:40.890
And Rei-chan won't tell me anything.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:42.630
Since it's come to this,

00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:44.260
we have no choice but to ask
Rosa Gigantea directly!

00:06:44.670 --> 00:06:46.720
Y-Yoshino-san, hold on a minute!

00:06:50.810 --> 00:06:52.330
I don't know either.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:54.430
I see.

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:57.670
I wonder if there really is no
choice but to ask Rosa Gigantea.

00:06:59.480 --> 00:07:01.280
Then, you can come with me, too.

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:03.710
Why?

00:07:04.420 --> 00:07:07.010
"Why?" You're her soeur, aren't you?

00:07:07.360 --> 00:07:08.520
Aren't you curious?

00:07:09.460 --> 00:07:10.080
No.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:14.820
More importantly, Yumi-san,

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:17.220
don't you think you had better get going?

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:18.020
What?

00:07:18.370 --> 00:07:19.870
If you don't hurry,

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.500
Rosa Gigantea will have
gone to the Rose Mansion.

00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:26.440
You can't ask this in front of
Rei-sama and Sachiko-sama, right?

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:28.630
Oh... right.

00:07:31.050 --> 00:07:33.380
Year 3, Wisteria Class, Miss Sato Sei,

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:36.940
please come to the Non-Curricular
Guidance Office immediately.

00:07:37.220 --> 00:07:39.350
This couldn't be about that novel, could it?

00:07:39.420 --> 00:07:40.510
Non-Curricular Guidance Office

00:07:45.890 --> 00:07:48.260
Oh? Did you get summoned too, Yumi-chan?

00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:50.660
Rosa Gigantea...

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:58.260
You didn't, by any chance, report me
for being a serial hugger, did you?

00:07:58.470 --> 00:08:01.600
Rosa Gigantea, are you not aware?

00:08:02.440 --> 00:08:03.380
Of what?

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:07.070
Um, I had meant to ask you about this, too.

00:08:07.450 --> 00:08:10.580
Whether you are the author of
"The Forest of Briars."

00:08:11.850 --> 00:08:12.650
Briars?

00:08:16.920 --> 00:08:19.790
Well, Yumi-chan, we'll continue this later.

00:08:23.660 --> 00:08:26.730
The Academy Director,
the principal of secondary education,

00:08:26.730 --> 00:08:29.400
the head teacher of Year 3, and the
Wisteria Class homeroom teacher...

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:32.630
I had no idea "The Forest of Briars"
was such a serious issue.

00:08:34.210 --> 00:08:34.940
Yumi-san.

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:37.630
Yoshino-san...

00:08:38.350 --> 00:08:39.680
How was Rosa Gigantea?

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:42.680
She was cheerful, like always.

00:08:42.680 --> 00:08:45.620
And it seemed like she didn't know
why she had been summoned.

00:08:45.620 --> 00:08:46.420
I see...

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:50.350
I wonder what's going to
happen to Rosa Gigantea...

00:08:54.600 --> 00:08:55.460
It's taking so long.

00:08:55.860 --> 00:08:56.490
Yes.

00:09:01.570 --> 00:09:02.590
Good afternoon.

00:09:03.800 --> 00:09:04.860
Good afternoon.
Good afternoon.

00:09:05.640 --> 00:09:10.600
But we know of nothing that might
be of interest to the school paper!

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:13.610
Don't say that. Work with me here.

00:09:14.280 --> 00:09:16.980
Don't you care if
Rosa Gigantea gets expelled?

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:18.290
Expelled?!

00:09:18.790 --> 00:09:21.250
Our school prohibits working part-time jobs.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:25.450
Writing a novel would be clearly
against school regulations.

00:09:26.390 --> 00:09:29.450
Surely... she wouldn't be expelled...

00:09:30.030 --> 00:09:34.700
If that happens, I could have the
Lillian Ledger run a petition drive.

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:38.740
Saying, "Please do not expel Rosa Gigantea."

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:40.980
But...

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:43.570
...we really don't know anything...

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:44.800
Really?

00:09:45.450 --> 00:09:46.440
Really...

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:49.310
Whoops.

00:09:49.750 --> 00:09:53.950
Sorry, I can't hold you any longer,
so could you step away?

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:55.720
Rosa Gigantea!

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:58.860
Besides, tumbling into the
Non-Curricular Guidance Office...

00:09:58.860 --> 00:10:00.760
...locked in each other's arms would be bad.

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:04.130
I'm sorry to have troubled you.

00:10:04.970 --> 00:10:06.260
Please excuse me.

00:10:09.970 --> 00:10:14.140
I'm sure you're dying to know, so I'll tell you,

00:10:14.140 --> 00:10:18.440
but unfortunately, I'm not the one who
wrote "The Forest of Briars," okay?

00:10:20.280 --> 00:10:22.750
So, I'm so sorry I wasn't able...

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:25.980
...to provide the Lillian Ledger
with a story this time,

00:10:26.420 --> 00:10:27.790
Tsukiyama Minako-san.

00:10:29.760 --> 00:10:31.220
So, shall we go?

00:10:31.990 --> 00:10:33.820
Where... to?

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:36.130
The Rose Mansion, of course.

00:10:36.800 --> 00:10:39.860
Everyone's probably waiting,
having heard the summons.

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:44.890
Maria Watches Over Us

00:10:49.110 --> 00:10:50.940
That was certainly an ostentatious summons.

00:10:51.980 --> 00:10:54.280
I've never been summoned personally,

00:10:54.450 --> 00:10:56.440
so I might be just a bit jealous.

00:10:56.980 --> 00:10:58.250
Why thank you.

00:11:02.120 --> 00:11:03.850
The Lady Roses certainly are impressive.

00:11:04.060 --> 00:11:07.050
I guess they don't act flustered like me...

00:11:11.270 --> 00:11:13.230
Were you at the Non-Curricular Guidance Office?

00:11:13.730 --> 00:11:14.330
Yes.

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:16.160
I see.

00:11:17.410 --> 00:11:18.170
Here you are.

00:11:19.070 --> 00:11:19.730
Thank you.

00:11:24.480 --> 00:11:25.780
Beautifully refined.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:29.640
Allow me to give you a little report.

00:11:30.150 --> 00:11:33.280
I already told Yumi-chan and Yoshino-chan this,

00:11:33.350 --> 00:11:35.250
but you know that novel
everyone's talking about?

00:11:35.460 --> 00:11:37.290
That's not me, okay?

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:38.380
That is all.

00:11:39.060 --> 00:11:41.190
That was the reason you were summoned?

00:11:41.830 --> 00:11:42.520
And?

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:44.290
Nothing really.

00:11:44.770 --> 00:11:46.800
When I plainly stated that it wasn't me,

00:11:46.800 --> 00:11:48.970
the Academy Director stood up for me...

00:11:48.970 --> 00:11:50.870
...and I was released, just like that.

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.540
I hadn't read the actual book myself...

00:11:53.970 --> 00:11:57.010
...and actually, the very fact that
such a rumor was floating about...

00:11:57.010 --> 00:11:58.040
...was something I found out just earlier.

00:11:58.610 --> 00:12:01.340
So, you really weren't the one who wrote it.

00:12:02.420 --> 00:12:04.280
I swear to Maria-sama.

00:12:05.690 --> 00:12:06.680
Understood.

00:12:07.320 --> 00:12:09.690
Then let us consider this matter closed.

00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:12.150
What do you say to that, Rosa Foetida?

00:12:13.790 --> 00:12:17.130
I have no objections, Rosa Chinensis.

00:12:17.900 --> 00:12:18.690
What?!

00:12:19.200 --> 00:12:21.900
Now, about the Christmas Party...

00:12:22.140 --> 00:12:22.930
Yes...

00:12:24.370 --> 00:12:27.600
I guess they don't let rumors get to them.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:31.670
I'm so low-brow and superficial.

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:33.070
It's depressing.

00:12:36.180 --> 00:12:39.210
What? Was I making a lot of funny faces again?!

00:12:40.520 --> 00:12:41.680
What is it, Yumi-chan?

00:12:42.060 --> 00:12:43.420
Do you have something to say?

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:45.880
Uh... no...

00:12:47.290 --> 00:12:48.230
Pardon me.

00:12:49.060 --> 00:12:50.790
Stay awake and keep your wits about you!

00:12:52.300 --> 00:12:53.930
If anyone has something to share,

00:12:53.930 --> 00:12:56.330
please make sure to raise your hand, okay?

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:00.330
To think I was worried about someone like her...

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:09.310
Please, stop this, Rosa Gigantea.

00:13:09.580 --> 00:13:12.140
Oh, dear. In a foul mood, are we?

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:15.180
Sachiko, let me borrow Yumi-chan.

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:19.420
I don't especially mind if you do, but...

00:13:19.860 --> 00:13:20.850
Don't worry.

00:13:21.100 --> 00:13:23.660
I won't strip her of her uniform
and toy with her or anything.

00:13:25.470 --> 00:13:28.700
Speak such nonsense and
I shall decline your request!

00:13:28.800 --> 00:13:29.700
Yes, ma'am.

00:13:30.470 --> 00:13:33.200
Oh, Rei, I'm going to borrow Yoshino-chan, too.

00:13:34.540 --> 00:13:36.010
As long as Yoshino doesn't mind.

00:13:37.910 --> 00:13:40.440
Are you sure you should give
your consent so easily?

00:13:41.180 --> 00:13:44.810
Rei knows that I won't do
anything naughty to Yoshino-chan.

00:13:45.450 --> 00:13:47.650
Uh... why just me?

00:13:49.020 --> 00:13:50.920
The way you react is great.

00:13:51.190 --> 00:13:53.460
Plus, I enjoy seeing how Sachiko responds.

00:13:55.460 --> 00:13:57.560
You soeurs are twice the enjoyment in one bite.

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:58.760
Thank you.

00:13:59.270 --> 00:14:00.330
I put my hands together.

00:14:00.330 --> 00:14:01.030
What?!

00:14:01.970 --> 00:14:04.900
I'm the only one who's fallen
prey to the evil upperclassman.

00:14:06.040 --> 00:14:09.240
So, the three of us will handle the clean-up.

00:14:09.440 --> 00:14:11.310
Ladies, please feel free to go on home.

00:14:11.550 --> 00:14:13.270
Then we'll leave the rest to you.

00:14:13.410 --> 00:14:14.240
Pardon us.

00:14:15.780 --> 00:14:19.650
Yumi, try not to entertain Rosa Gigantea.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:21.610
I-I will!

00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:26.290
Onee-sama, is there anything I can help with?

00:14:27.190 --> 00:14:29.490
Nothing especially comes to mind...

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:31.120
I see.

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:33.620
Then, I shall go on home.

00:14:34.240 --> 00:14:36.730
I'm sorry for making you keep
my Onee-sama company.

00:14:37.200 --> 00:14:38.100
Good day.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:44.270
Was there something wrong
with Shimako-san joining us?

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:45.510
If she wanted to stay,

00:14:45.510 --> 00:14:48.680
Shimako is the kind of girl
who'll stay of her own will,

00:14:48.680 --> 00:14:51.010
even when she's told not to.

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:56.090
So, Yumi-chan, do you have
"The Forest of Briars" on you right now?

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:58.720
Oh, uh... yes.

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:00.330
Would you lend it to me?

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:03.590
I don't mind, but what are you going to do?

00:15:04.000 --> 00:15:05.630
Read it, of course.

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:09.060
Did you think that I'd turn it
into a hot pad or something?

00:15:09.740 --> 00:15:10.470
Here you are.

00:15:11.610 --> 00:15:12.540
Very good.

00:15:12.970 --> 00:15:14.240
And in exchange...

00:15:15.810 --> 00:15:17.540
Meal tickets from the noodle cafeteria?

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:19.480
You two go together.

00:15:20.080 --> 00:15:20.840
But...

00:15:21.280 --> 00:15:24.010
On your way back, buy me a can
of coffee from a vending machine.

00:15:24.650 --> 00:15:26.380
You can buy drinks for yourselves too.

00:15:27.790 --> 00:15:28.280
All right.

00:15:29.660 --> 00:15:31.890
Rosa Gigantea is inscrutable.

00:15:32.360 --> 00:15:33.120
Yes...

00:15:33.760 --> 00:15:35.660
Shimako-san is incredible, don't you think?

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:38.260
Being soeur to someone like that...

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:43.140
Oh, Yumi-san, you might want to tuck
a handkerchief in at your neck.

00:15:43.370 --> 00:15:44.500
Your collar's going to get soiled.

00:15:45.310 --> 00:15:45.930
Yes...

00:15:47.010 --> 00:15:47.840
What's wrong?

00:15:48.680 --> 00:15:52.810
I wonder why Rosa Gigantea
detained the two of us.

00:15:52.980 --> 00:15:53.570
What?

00:15:54.180 --> 00:15:57.150
I mean, if it's just to read
"The Forest of Briars,"

00:15:57.150 --> 00:15:58.980
she could easily take it home.

00:16:00.220 --> 00:16:00.650
Oh!

00:16:01.420 --> 00:16:04.880
Maybe she wanted to treat us to
ramen because we're so cute?!

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.820
Yumi-san, your brain must be melted...

00:16:12.900 --> 00:16:14.730
There is no way!

00:16:14.840 --> 00:16:15.730
You think so?

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:18.170
No normal person buys sweet red
bean soup with rice cake in a can!

00:16:18.170 --> 00:16:19.200
What does it matter?!

00:16:20.010 --> 00:16:21.910
Oh, pardon us for making you wait.

00:16:22.740 --> 00:16:25.610
What's this about sweet red bean
soup with rice cakes in a can?

00:16:25.880 --> 00:16:26.850
Hey! Sweet Red Bean
Soup With Rice Cake
Green Tea Flavor

00:16:26.850 --> 00:16:28.370
Hey! Sweet Red Bean
Soup With Rice Cake
Green Tea Flavor
Yumi-san bought it.

00:16:29.120 --> 00:16:30.240
What is this?!

00:16:30.750 --> 00:16:32.880
I had no idea such a thing even existed!

00:16:35.120 --> 00:16:39.220
Here! We made sure to buy coffee for you.

00:16:39.860 --> 00:16:40.790
Thank you.

00:16:42.930 --> 00:16:44.760
Did you actually read the book?

00:16:45.530 --> 00:16:46.230
I did.

00:16:46.970 --> 00:16:48.730
That person might have a pretty good instinct.

00:16:49.370 --> 00:16:52.640
Whoever started the rumor that I wrote
"The Forest of Briars."

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:53.710
What?
What?

00:16:55.010 --> 00:16:57.640
I mean, she's similar to me, isn't she?

00:16:58.310 --> 00:16:59.240
You can ask.

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:03.050
You must have some notion
that it's not just my name...

00:17:03.050 --> 00:17:05.610
...that caused people to attribute
the writing of this novel to me.

00:17:06.790 --> 00:17:10.690
Have we been so openly curious?

00:17:11.660 --> 00:17:15.060
I didn't say that to make you hang your heads...

00:17:15.730 --> 00:17:18.250
I won't tell you the parts
I don't want to talk about,

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:19.760
but if you're fine with that...

00:17:20.730 --> 00:17:21.720
Why?

00:17:22.270 --> 00:17:25.400
Because it's not fair that you're
the only ones who don't know.

00:17:25.640 --> 00:17:26.500
In a vague sort of way...

00:17:26.910 --> 00:17:30.240
Did you detain us so that you could tell us?

00:17:30.740 --> 00:17:33.440
Part of it was that I wanted
to read it in short order.

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:36.640
The reason Yoko, Rei, and the
others won't explain it to you...

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:39.810
...is probably because they
want to respect my feelings.

00:17:41.520 --> 00:17:43.990
It goes to show just how painful
the incident must have been...

00:17:44.360 --> 00:17:47.850
I had a really good friend, you see.

00:17:48.360 --> 00:17:51.400
So good, I cherished her more
than my parents or siblings...

00:17:51.400 --> 00:17:52.600
...and I loved her so much,

00:17:52.600 --> 00:17:54.930
I felt like if I just had her,
I didn't need anything else.

00:17:56.100 --> 00:18:00.470
She was a pure person,
who was thinking of becoming a nun,

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:04.340
but last year, on Christmas Day, I lost her.

00:18:05.250 --> 00:18:06.510
What?! Then...

00:18:06.510 --> 00:18:10.180
That is exactly the same as Sei and
Kaori in "The Forest of Briars."

00:18:10.780 --> 00:18:12.840
It's not exactly the same.

00:18:13.490 --> 00:18:17.750
I never left on a journey with her.

00:18:18.390 --> 00:18:20.660
Nor did we take sleeping pills.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:23.150
She transferred schools.

00:18:23.530 --> 00:18:26.160
Then, Kaori-san is alive?

00:18:27.000 --> 00:18:28.200
What's this?

00:18:28.200 --> 00:18:29.860
Are you disappointed that she's alive?

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:31.490
Pardon me.

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:38.310
Then, could someone have based this
novel on what happened to you?

00:18:39.050 --> 00:18:40.240
It's hard to say.

00:18:40.810 --> 00:18:42.850
Some parts are different,

00:18:42.850 --> 00:18:45.320
while other parts are startlingly similar.

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:48.510
Doesn't it make you angry, Rosa Gigantea?!

00:18:48.860 --> 00:18:51.790
Having your past turned into a
novel without your permission...

00:18:51.790 --> 00:18:53.990
Not to mention being mistaken
for being the author!

00:18:54.960 --> 00:18:59.730
I'm fine, as long as the people
I care about understand.

00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:02.660
That's why I wanted to tell you two.

00:19:03.200 --> 00:19:05.010
Because I don't want any relationships...

00:19:05.010 --> 00:19:06.600
...with lingering misunderstandings
or speculations.

00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:12.210
Your friend, who transferred...
How is she doing now?

00:19:13.480 --> 00:19:16.380
Oh, who knows how she's doing?

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:18.880
Don't you want to see her?

00:19:19.950 --> 00:19:21.940
It's better that I don't.

00:19:22.990 --> 00:19:25.980
Her name isn't Kaori.

00:19:27.590 --> 00:19:29.790
It's Kubo Shiori.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:38.570
Rosa Gigantea must still have
feelings for that person.

00:19:39.040 --> 00:19:39.700
Yes.

00:19:40.640 --> 00:19:42.130
I got that impression, too.

00:19:42.810 --> 00:19:45.440
I wonder if that's why
she didn't detain Shimako-san.

00:19:45.910 --> 00:19:47.470
Because it's not nice to Shimako-san.

00:19:49.950 --> 00:19:51.280
I find it unforgivable somehow.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:54.220
The writing of this story can
be hurtful to some people.

00:19:55.490 --> 00:19:56.460
Yoshino-san?

00:19:57.290 --> 00:20:01.160
It couldn't be Kubo Shiori-san
who wrote that novel, could it?

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:02.120
What?

00:20:02.260 --> 00:20:03.590
All right! I've made up my mind!

00:20:03.860 --> 00:20:06.490
I'm going to track down the person
who wrote "The Forest of Briars"!

00:20:06.970 --> 00:20:07.930
What?!

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:16.600
So this is Cosmos' editorial department...

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:18.810
Why am I here too?

00:20:19.110 --> 00:20:21.170
You want to know too, don't you?

00:20:21.350 --> 00:20:23.340
About who wrote "The Forest of Briars"?

00:20:23.650 --> 00:20:24.670
Yes, but...

00:20:26.920 --> 00:20:28.010
Pardon me for making you wait.

00:20:28.320 --> 00:20:30.260
We are sorry to disturb you
when you must be busy.

00:20:30.260 --> 00:20:32.850
Um, you handled the publishing of
"The Forest of Briars," correct?

00:20:33.490 --> 00:20:34.860
Yes, that's right,

00:20:35.300 --> 00:20:38.290
but I cannot reveal Suga Sei's identity.

00:20:38.630 --> 00:20:39.260
What?

00:20:40.330 --> 00:20:41.940
These last couple days,

00:20:41.940 --> 00:20:44.900
we've received inquiry after inquiry
from Lillian's students.

00:20:45.340 --> 00:20:48.210
Asking if Suga Sei's true
identity is Sato Sei-san.

00:20:50.580 --> 00:20:51.310
Sasaki-san?

00:20:52.280 --> 00:20:53.540
S-Sensei!

00:20:55.650 --> 00:20:58.680
My! Those uniforms bring back such memories!

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:02.620
What an unexpected pleasure to run into
students from my old school here!

00:21:02.620 --> 00:21:03.560
Sensei!

00:21:04.020 --> 00:21:07.520
Oh, then are you an alumna of Lillian?

00:21:08.400 --> 00:21:10.990
Yes, from a long time ago.

00:21:13.300 --> 00:21:14.130
Then...

00:21:14.130 --> 00:21:14.830
Are you?!

00:21:15.700 --> 00:21:18.830
I am Kasuga Seiko, also known as Suga Sei.

00:21:19.340 --> 00:21:22.400
Then, even though "The Forest of Briars"
does take place at Lillian...

00:21:22.810 --> 00:21:24.940
It means the story is from a long time ago?

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:29.280
"The Forest of Briars" was an incident
that happened so long ago,

00:21:29.280 --> 00:21:31.380
there were not even any lingering rumors of it.

00:21:32.120 --> 00:21:35.380
Entirely unrelated to Rosa Gigantea's tale...

00:21:39.590 --> 00:21:41.360
I hadn't spoken it in a long time...

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:43.430
Her name...

00:21:56.480 --> 00:21:57.670
Are you a new student?

00:21:59.380 --> 00:22:02.970
Yes. I just enrolled at Lillian this year.

00:22:04.650 --> 00:22:05.620
What's your name?

00:23:22.130 --> 00:23:22.700
Preview

00:23:22.700 --> 00:23:25.570
Preview
Onee-sama, what is the "bira" in
"hanabira (petals)"? The " bira" part.

00:23:25.570 --> 00:23:26.370
Preview
The strangest things catch
your attention, don't they?

00:23:26.370 --> 00:23:27.570
The strangest things catch
your attention, don't they?

00:23:27.570 --> 00:23:30.270
The "bira" in " hanabira" is the kanji
for "ben" in " bento (boxed lunch)."

00:23:30.270 --> 00:23:31.610
The "ben" in " bento," is it?

00:23:31.610 --> 00:23:32.470
I see, so it's the "ben" in " bento."

00:23:32.470 --> 00:23:33.370
Next Time
I see, so it's the "ben" in " bento."
"The White Petals"

00:23:33.370 --> 00:23:36.340
Next Time
We have a beautiful story next week.
I feel like this is spoiling it.
"The White Petals"

00:23:36.340 --> 00:23:36.810
Next Time
"The White Petals"
